WEBVTT

00:00:01.500 --> 00:00:06.180
Every morning, a big riverside school in the forest of Borneo comes to life.
每天早上，婆罗洲森林里一所很大的河畔学校都会热闹起来。

00:00:06.980 --> 00:00:17.440
The caretakers and teachers in the school are from a specialized team, and the students there are orangutans whose parents have gone missing, making it one of the most unusual schools in the world.
这所学校的看护员和老师都来自一支专业团队，这里的学生则是父母已经失踪的猩猩，这使它成为世界上最不寻常的学校之一。

00:00:18.240 --> 00:00:23.440
The orangutans aged from 2 to 8 are divided into five groups according to their skills.
2到8岁的猩猩按照各自的技能分成五组。

00:00:24.240 --> 00:00:29.660
They are looked after by the team who feed the babies and teach the older ones to start feeding themselves.
它们由这支团队照顾：队员们给幼崽喂食，还教大一些的猩猩开始自己进食。

00:00:30.460 --> 00:00:32.370
There are often problems in the beginning.
一开始常常会出现问题。

00:00:33.170 --> 00:00:38.520
For example, there was a lesson about how to break open a coconut to drink the milk inside.
比如，有一节课讲的是怎样把椰子敲开，喝里面的椰汁。

00:00:39.320 --> 00:00:44.230
Several young orangutans couldn’t do that and they got very angry about the whole thing.
有几只小猩猩做不到这一点，为这整件事非常生气。

00:00:45.030 --> 00:00:50.700
Of course, as in any social group, the orangutans have to learn to get on with each other.
当然，就像在任何社会群体中一样，猩猩们必须学会彼此和睦相处。

00:00:51.500 --> 00:00:56.660
There are the usual arguments over food when one orangutan doesn’t get what he or she wants.
一只猩猩得不到自己想要的东西时，就会为食物发生争吵，这是常有的事。

00:00:57.460 --> 00:01:01.630
However, with the care of the trainers, they gradually learn to accept each other.
不过，在训练员的照料下，它们会渐渐学会接纳彼此。

00:01:02.430 --> 00:01:06.520
In one of the lessons, the trainers taught young orangutans to climb trees.
在其中一节课上，训练员教小猩猩们爬树。

00:01:07.320 --> 00:01:09.650
This is an important skill they need to learn.
这是它们需要学会的一项重要技能。

00:01:10.450 --> 00:01:13.560
Some of the orangutans in particular were really scared.
尤其是其中一些猩猩，真的很害怕。

00:01:14.360 --> 00:01:22.410
It took them a long time to get the courage to climb up and swing from a branch, but when they finally did it, they were so satisfied with themselves!
它们花了很长时间，才鼓起勇气爬上去，吊在树枝上荡来荡去；但终于做到的时候，它们对自己满意极了！

00:01:23.210 --> 00:01:30.378
The goal of the “education system” is to train the orangutans to be able to live in the wild again and look after themselves.
这套“教育体系”的目标，是训练猩猩，让它们能够重新在野外生活，自己照顾自己。

00:01:31.178 --> 00:01:33.068
They won’t have to stay at school forever.
它们不必永远待在学校里。

00:01:33.868 --> 00:01:40.008
After the older orangutans are set free into the forest, there is no more connection with the people from the school.
年龄大一些的猩猩放归森林以后，就不再和学校的人有联系了。

00:01:40.808 --> 00:01:47.258
They now have to live as wild orangutans again and be accepted by the other orangutans who are already there.
现在，它们必须重新作为野生猩猩生活，还要让已经在那里的其他猩猩接纳自己。

00:01:48.058 --> 00:01:50.388
The day when they say goodbye is a difficult one.
告别的那一天，是难熬的一天。

00:01:51.188 --> 00:01:53.898
However, the trainers are happy that their job is done.
不过，训练员们很高兴自己的工作完成了。

00:01:54.698 --> 00:01:59.968
They have successfully taught young orangutans how to live in the wild again—where they belong.
他们已经成功地教会了小猩猩怎样重新在野外生活——它们本来就属于那里。
